#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Above: winoracle (WARP, Windows 11, fxc 10.1 / SDK 10.0.26100) output of
# dbl64.exe dbl.cfg -- the area-09a runner (d3d11_a09a_alu_probe.c) over
# d3d11_doubles_shaders.hlsl and d3d11_doubles_gen_input.py's words -- built
# and run by tools/oracle_probe/d3d11_doubles_build.sh (CR dropped). The x86
# runner (dbl32.exe) differs only in NaN payload bits of dbin (both-NaN
# operands), which D3D11.3 3.1.3.2 leaves free. Re-running reproduces this
# file byte for byte.
#
# WARP vs D3D11.3 (3.1.4, 22.14-22.17), classified word by word against the
# reference model tests/graphics/double_probe_model.h (host IEEE doubles):
#   exact everywhere except
#   - per-thread dtoi/dtou/itod (dun cols 3/4, dconv/dvec/dmod itod, dmod
#     dtoi/dtou): WARP applies ANOTHER lane's clamp or sign decision
#     (123456789.123 -> 0x80000000, itod(-1) -> +1.0). The lane-uniform
#     rows (duni/iuni: all 64 lanes convert one value) are spec-exact for
#     dtoi and itod/utod.
#   - dtou next to 2^31 even lane-uniform (duni col 1, 5 words:
#     2147483649.0 -> 0x80000000, 2147483647.99976 -> 0x7ffffffe).
#   - dfma at the extremes (dbin/fmauni 30, dmod 2): addend-dominated
#     results come out halved (fma(2^53, 0.99.., 0.5) -> 2^52), and a
#     product that overflows before an infinite addend gives NaN (drnd
#     col 10/11, 37) -- not the single rounding 22.14.7 requires.
#   - NaN payloads (any NaN is legal): a NaN operand is returned quieted,
#     the first in source order (WARP x64 returns -b's for dadd a, -b when
#     both are NaN); invalid operations give 0xFFF8000000000000.
#   Choices the spec leaves open, taken from here: dmin/dmax of equal
#   operands (+0/-0) return src1, both NaN src0; drcp correctly rounded;
#   dtof keeps float denormals. p_dimm1 (patched): a ONE-component
#   Immediate64 is two DWORDs and WARP reads the first into every component
#   (dmov r1.xy, <0x3fb999999999999a> -> 9999999a 9999999a).
#   _sat (p_dsat, patched on every instruction):
#   double results NaN->+0, <0->+0 but -0 kept, >=1->1.0; dtof_sat a float
#   saturate flushing denormals and -0; deq..dne/dtoi/dtou ignore it.
#
# Vitreo (build 2026-09-28, doubles pass): 1717 diff lines x64 and x86 (x86
# vs its own WARP run: 1703): adapter, feature level (11_0), min-precision
# caps, the fnv lines, and exactly the WARP defects and NaN payload words
# above; every Vitreo word equals the D3D11.3 answer
# (tests/graphics/test_shader_double_gpu.cpp runs the same shaders on Metal).
